  "name": "Northwest Pacific Moored Sediment Trap Data - Russian Collaboration, 1991-1992",
  "description": "Time series data from 3 moored sediment traps deployed in the NW Pacific Ocean in 1991-1992 at 4000-5000m. Collaborative data collected on Russian vessels.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Biogeochemical flux in the deep ocean.\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Custodian will be leaving soon and has a large quantity of data not secured in a regional data centre. Risk of Loss: High Impact Justification: Does not affect a wide variety of users. Impact of Loss: Low Recommended Action: Bring data to archives. Additional Info: See also entry under, Northwest Pacific, 1991-1992 (GEMS); data from cruises to deploy and retrieve sediment traps. Four sediment traps were deployed; one did not work.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570824",
